[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3027438823","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108197#issuecomment-3027438823","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108197","id":3027438823,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc60cwzn","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-02T11:04:57Z","updated_at":"2025-07-02T11:04:57Z","body":"I'm not sure this particular syntax was ever intended to work, I'd consider the code in question wrong and I'd not expect it to work at any time, bodyless lambas were never explicitly permitted I don't think","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3027438823/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3027692701","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108197#issuecomment-3027692701","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108197","id":3027692701,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc60duyd","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-02T12:28:49Z","updated_at":"2025-07-02T12:42:34Z","body":"This also affects cases calling a method, like:\n```gdscript\nready.connect(func():)\n```\n\nHowever doing the same with a variable throws the correct error (Expected indented block after lambda declaration):\n```gdscript\nvar my_call = func():\n```\n\nIMO the solution here is to ensure a proper clear error message here","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3027692701/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3027902490","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108197#issuecomment-3027902490","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108197","id":3027902490,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc60eiAa","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-02T13:30:57Z","updated_at":"2025-07-02T13:36:07Z","body":"```GDScript\nfunc _hide_modal(delay: float = 0, callback: Callable = func() -> void: pass) -> void:\n\tpass\n```\nThis works fine.\nAlthough I suppose this would be even better:\n\n```GDScript\nfunc _hide_modal(delay: float = 0, callback: Callable = func() -> Variant: return null) -> void:\n\tpass\n```","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3027902490/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3027913725","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108197#issuecomment-3027913725","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108197","id":3027913725,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc60ekv9","user":{"login":"timothyqiu","id":372476,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MjQ3Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/372476?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu","html_url":"https://github.com/timothyqiu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-02T13:34:35Z","updated_at":"2025-07-02T13:37:53Z","body":"You can also add `pass` as the function's body:\n\n```gdscript\nfunc _hide_modal(delay: float = 0, callback: Callable = func():pass) -> void:\n```\n\nI'm a bit surprised that it _just works_™ in old versions ;)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3027913725/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3028153644","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108197#issuecomment-3028153644","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108197","id":3028153644,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc60ffUs","user":{"login":"goranovs","id":2466340,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NjYzNDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2466340?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goranovs","html_url":"https://github.com/goranovs","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goranovs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goranovs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goranovs/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goranovs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goranovs/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goranovs/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goranovs/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goranovs/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goranovs/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-02T14:44:38Z","updated_at":"2025-07-02T14:44:38Z","body":"> I'm not sure this particular syntax was ever intended to work\n\nI agree. I was still learning GDScript when I wrote this code. I remember trying it both with and without pass, and since it worked either way, I ended up removing it.\n\nMaybe the error message should just change the \"abstract\" part in this specific case, since you actually can’t use `@abstract` there anyway.\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3028153644/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3028508195","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108197#issuecomment-3028508195","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108197","id":3028508195,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc60g14j","user":{"login":"MarianoGnu","id":1776044,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzYwNDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1776044?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu","html_url":"https://github.com/MarianoGnu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-02T16:31:02Z","updated_at":"2025-07-02T17:35:15Z","body":"having an empty function is a little uncanny to me.\n\nIf the function is optional i'd go with:\n\n```\nfunc _hide_modal(delay: float = 0, callback := Callable():) -> void:\n\t# some stuff\n\tif callback.is_valid():\n\t\tcallback.call()\n```\n\n> Maybe the error message should just change the \"abstract\" part in this specific case, since you actually can’t use `@abstract` there anyway.\n\nAlso, doesn't abstract syntaxt requires the funciton to not have a : (colon) at the end of the declaration?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3028508195/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3064663735","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108197#issuecomment-3064663735","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108197","id":3064663735,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62qw63","user":{"login":"tavurth","id":100964,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDk2NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100964?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tavurth","html_url":"https://github.com/tavurth","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tavurth/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tavurth/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tavurth/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tavurth/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tavurth/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tavurth/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tavurth/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tavurth/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tavurth/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-12T04:23:22Z","updated_at":"2025-07-12T04:25:12Z","body":"```gdscript\nfunc noop() -> void:\n        pass\n\nfunc _hide_modal(delay: float = 0, callback := Callable(noop)) -> void:\n\t# some stuff\n\tif callback.is_valid():\n\t\tcallback.call()\n```\n\nThe original code breaking does seem like expected behaviour. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3064663735/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3134526403","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108197#issuecomment-3134526403","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108197","id":3134526403,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc661RPD","user":{"login":"Shadows-of-Fire","id":3682588,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODI1ODg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3682588?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire","html_url":"https://github.com/Shadows-of-Fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-30T00:49:46Z","updated_at":"2025-07-30T00:49:46Z","body":"Given that Godot has an established convention that functions with an empty body are ill-formed, I would expect the code to break.\n\nI think it _should_ break. Though, I also think that the syntax `callback: Callable = func(): pass` is a bit hard to parse since it _looks_ remarkably similar to the variable declaration syntax. \n\nSimilarly, the expected full-fat syntax `callback: Callable = func() -> void: pass` also doesn't fit well in this context. It would get even more verbose if `Callable` had generics.\n\nNaively, the most straightforward solution would be to add a static variable `Callable.EMPTY` (or, more forward thinking, a static method `Callable.empty()` which returns the field that can be upgraded to support generics later) as a sentinel.\n\nThen you could write `callback: Callable = Callback.empty()` (or `callback := Callback.empty()`, not sure if function-default parameters support `:=`).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3134526403/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3135708542","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108197#issuecomment-3135708542","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108197","id":3135708542,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc665x1-","user":{"login":"goranovs","id":2466340,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NjYzNDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2466340?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goranovs","html_url":"https://github.com/goranovs","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goranovs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goranovs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goranovs/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goranovs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goranovs/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goranovs/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goranovs/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goranovs/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goranovs/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-30T10:24:36Z","updated_at":"2025-07-30T10:24:36Z","body":"I personaly will use this approach as it just works™️ for all my cases (for now 🤷‍♂️).\n```gdscript\nfunc with_callback(_flag: bool = false, callback: Callable = Callable()) -> void:\n\tprints(callback)\n\t\n\tif callback.is_valid():\n\t\tcallback.call()\n\n\nfunc with_callback_short(_flag:= false, callback:= Callable()) -> void:\n\tprints(callback)\n\t\n\tif callback:\n\t\tcallback.call()\n```\n<details>\n<summary>Example</summary>\n\n  ```gdscript\n  \twith_callback()\n  \twith_callback(false)\n  \twith_callback(true, func():\n  \t\tprints(\"Call <anonymous lambda>!\")\n  \t)\n  \twith_callback(true, my_callback)\n  \twith_callback(true, my_callback_with_arguments.bind(1))\n  # ...\n  \n  func my_callback() -> void:\n  \tprints(\"Call my_callback!\")\n  \n  \n  func my_callback_with_arguments(number: int) -> void:\n  \tprints(\"Call my_callback_with_arguments!\", number)\n  ```\n</details>\n\nFeel free to close this as it seems the reported issue is expected.\n\nThe only thing that is a bit wierd to me is the error, but that can be another issue.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Some thoughts about the error message</summary>\n\nIn any node script(not abstract class) if you skip the `:`  the error is `A function must either have a \":\" followed by a body, or be marked as \"@abstract\".` \n```gdscript\nextends Node2D\n\nfunc not_abstract()\n```\n IMO it should say only `A function must have a \":\" followed by a body`.\n\nif you add the `@abstract` as suggested you get `Class \"node_2d.gd\" is not abstract but contains abstract methods. Mark the class as \"@abstract\" or remove \"@abstract\" from all methods in this class.`\n\nIn abstract class\n```gdscript\n@abstract class Abstracted:\n\t@abstract func abstracted():\n```\nIf you add extra `:` the error is `Expected indented block after function declaration.`\nand if you add body to resolve the error you get `Abstract function cannot have a body.` \n\nPerhaps the first error must say `Abstract function cannot have a \":\" and body.`\n\n</details>","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3135708542/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3180255171","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108197#issuecomment-3180255171","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108197","id":3180255171,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc69jtfD","user":{"login":"vnen","id":5599796,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1OTk3OTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5599796?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vnen","html_url":"https://github.com/vnen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vnen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vnen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vnen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vnen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vnen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vnen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vnen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vnen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vnen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-12T17:10:06Z","updated_at":"2025-08-12T17:10:06Z","body":"Discussed in the GDScript meeting. The consensus is that the original behavior is a bug, lambdas shouldn't have empty bodies (you can use `pass` if needed). However, the error message need to be improved.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3180255171/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3180284512","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108197#issuecomment-3180284512","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108197","id":3180284512,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc69j0pg","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id"